WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:06.777
"I see the Valentine's Day cards," Mom said.

2
00:00:06.778 --> 00:00:09.967
The Carter family was at the store.

3
00:00:09.968 --> 00:00:13.265
They were shopping for cards.

4
00:00:13.266 --> 00:00:17.869
Everything was pink or red.

5
00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:21.181
Hearts were everywhere.

6
00:00:21.182 --> 00:00:28.003
Harry groaned. "Valentine's Day is so dumb."

7
00:00:28.004 --> 00:00:32.911
"Oh, come on, Harry." Emmy giggled.

8
00:00:32.912 --> 00:00:36.821
"Don't you have a valentine?"

9
00:00:36.822 --> 00:00:45.625
"No!" Harry made a face. "Gross!"

10
00:00:45.626 --> 00:00:49.746
Most cards came with stickers or candy.

11
00:00:49.747 --> 00:00:54.788
Oliver found some with gel pens.

12
00:00:54.789 --> 00:00:57.466
Mom shook her head.

13
00:00:57.467 --> 00:01:03.451
"Those are too expensive."

14
00:01:03.452 --> 00:01:07.661
"Did you find any cards, Harry?" Dad asked.

15
00:01:07.662 --> 00:01:11.282
"No," Harry said.

16
00:01:11.283 --> 00:01:15.457
"All these cards have goofy hearts."

17
00:01:15.458 --> 00:01:19.002
Emmy picked out one big card.

18
00:01:19.003 --> 00:01:22.597
"Who's that for?" Oliver asked.

19
00:01:22.598 --> 00:01:28.511
Emmy blushed. "I'm not telling you."

20
00:01:28.512 --> 00:01:31.973
Harry found cards with superheroes.

21
00:01:31.974 --> 00:01:34.117
"Even these have dumb hearts.

22
00:01:34.118 --> 00:01:37.479
But I guess they're okay."

23
00:01:37.480 --> 00:01:41.177
Finally it was Valentine's Day.

24
00:01:41.178 --> 00:01:46.353
"Valentine's Day is so dumb," Harry grumbled.

25
00:01:46.354 --> 00:01:48.577
Mom smiled.

26
00:01:48.578 --> 00:01:54.175
"Enjoy your class party," she said.

27
00:01:54.176 --> 00:01:56.952
Later Harry came home.

28
00:01:56.953 --> 00:02:02.097
He had a bag of valentines from his friends.

29
00:02:02.098 --> 00:02:05.758
"How was the party?" Mom asked.

30
00:02:05.759 --> 00:02:10.320
"Great!" Harry said.

31
00:02:10.321 --> 00:02:13.144
"Really?" Mom said.

32
00:02:13.145 --> 00:02:16.754
"I thought you didn't like Valentine's Day."

33
00:02:16.755 --> 00:02:20.803
Then she saw a big card in Harry's hand.

34
00:02:20.804 --> 00:02:24.052
Harry quickly hid it behind him.

35
00:02:24.053 --> 00:02:26.520
He grinned.

36
00:02:26.521 --> 00:02:32.643
"I think I like Valentine's Day after all!"

